WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.128
Can an AI

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:01.706
make a slinky

00:00:01.517 --> 00:00:02.248
walk down an

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:02.838
escalator

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:04.698
One prompt sent

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.052
once

00:00:05.229 --> 00:00:06.573
a single HTML

00:00:06.385 --> 00:00:07.057
file of a

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.425
rainbow slinky walking

00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:08.908
down an up

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.474
escalator

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:10.783
with real physics

00:00:10.878 --> 00:00:11.797
not a scripted

00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:12.469
animation

00:00:13.006 --> 00:00:14.303
Fifteen models from

00:00:14.126 --> 00:00:14.975
Anthropic

00:00:15.034 --> 00:00:16.508
OpenAI and Google

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:16.980
tried it through

00:00:16.791 --> 00:00:18.371
Codex Claude Code

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.444
and Antigravity

00:00:19.657 --> 00:00:20.553
recorded on a

00:00:20.364 --> 00:00:21.661
fixed 60 hertz

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:22.121
clock

00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:24.025
Several still cheated

00:00:24.085 --> 00:00:24.851
speeding up the

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:25.582
escalator

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.454
adding a torque

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:27.704
assist or resetting

00:00:27.516 --> 00:00:28.730
a stalled slinky

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:29.907
The author calls

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:30.791
it an anecdotal

00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:31.381
gut check

00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:32.916
Full story on

00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:33.623
the dashboard
